# Runtime files written by the game servers on first boot.
#
# Strategy: ignore everything inside server*/ by default, then explicitly
# un-ignore the small seed files we *do* want to track (eula.txt,
# server.properties, spigot.yml with bungeecord=true, and the paper-global
# proxies override). The eula.txt + server.properties give Paper enough to
# boot without prompting; spigot.yml + paper-global.yml fix the BungeeCord
# IP-forwarding handshake.

server*/*
!server*/eula.txt
!server*/server.properties
!server*/spigot.yml
!server*/config/
server*/config/*
!server*/config/paper-global.yml

# Master working dir is tiny — nothing to keep yet, but anything Paper
# would write here (logs, world data) is generated. Track only the
# placeholder config.
master/*
!master/multipaper-server.yml
